cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "newton-instrumentation: low-cost instrumentation for a 130/650 Newtonian"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software

authors:
  - given-names: David
    family-names: Conesa Pagán
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-9942-884X"
    affiliation: "Universidad Politécnica de Cartagena (UPCT)"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Dacongan/newton-instrumentation"
license: CERN-OHL-W-2.0

abstract: >-
  Open-hardware instrumentation for a Bresser 130/650 Newtonian
  reflector: active primary-mirror cooling, closed-loop secondary dew
  control referenced to the dew point, and a motorised focuser with
  3.13 um resolution. All parts are generated by parametric Rhino Python
  scripts and 3D-printed. The design is validated experimentally rather
  than by simulation: four DS18B20 probes record the thermal history of
  the mirror, secondary, internal air and ambient, and the resulting
  optical improvement is quantified as a Strehl ratio measured with the
  strehl planetary processing suite.

keywords:
  - astronomy
  - astrophotography
  - newtonian-telescope
  - open-hardware
  - instrumentation
  - thermal-control
  - 3d-printing
  - esp32
  - embedded-systems
  - parametric-design

